            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0336" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/2130</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 5 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>644. Department’s 516, [June] 8. Spanish Ambassador, Vienna, reports that
                    Austro-Hungarian Government agrees to allow Americans from Turkey to pass
                    through Austria-Hungary without fixing time limit, on condition that Austrian
                    representative, Constantinople, issue personal certificate in each individual
                    case. The Spanish Minister in Constantinople has been informed of above
                    agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
